#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# find_generating_function

#% text
# `find_generating_function(a, x)` gives a rational function whose power series in x has the coefficients a1, a2, ... of the list a.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The shortest linear recurrence with constant coefficients that the terms satisfy (checked on at least one term beyond those that determine it) gives the denominator; the numerator is the truncated product.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
find_generating_function([1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13], x)
#% output
#= (1 - x - x^2)^-1

#% cell
together(find_generating_function([0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0], x))
#% output
#= (-x - 2*x^2)/(-1 + x^3)

#% cell
together(find_generating_function([3, 7, 13, 21, 31, 43, 57], x))
#% output
#= (-3 + 2*x - x^2)/(-1 + 3*x - 3*x^2 + x^3)

#% cell
series(find_generating_function([1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13], x), x, 0, 9)
#% output
#= 1 + x + 2*x^2 + 3*x^3 + 5*x^4 + 8*x^5 + 13*x^6 + 21*x^7 + 34*x^8 + 55*x^9 + O(x^10)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `generating_function`, `find_sequence_function`, `series`
